same idea, same form. paired names for paired acts — open/close,
encode/decode; parallel branches in parallel shape. the reader reads one,
skims the other, and the difference is all that is left to read.
a symmetry broken is a case missing or a bug — or a special case the
design should have absorbed.

the test: diff the pair. what differs should be the only difference.

`programming/dry` rules the fact, this the form — alike in form, apart in
fact, is fine.
